{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsupports\/element"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSupports\/element"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"element","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLSupportsV7elementSSvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"element"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSupports"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"element"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"element"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The name of the MusicXML element for which support is being indicated."}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSupports":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLSupports","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSupports"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSupports"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The supports type indicates if a MusicXML encoding supports a particular MusicXML element. This is recommended","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for elements like beam, stem, and accidental, where the absence of an element is ambiguous if you do not know","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"if the encoding supports that element. For Version 2.0, the supports element is expanded to allow programs to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicate support for particular attributes or particular values. This lets applications communicate, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, that all system and\/or page breaks are contained in the MusicXML file.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsupports","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSupports","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSupports/element":{"kind":"symbol","title":"element","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSupports\/element","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsupports\/element","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"element"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The name of the MusicXML element for which support is being indicated."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}